 "guidance": [
  "goal giver at the spawn with the S in view (LP4 4:06:09)",
  "ride landmarks (ferris wheel, spinning bowl, coaster, castle flames, water tower) anchor navigation",
  "each ride ticket is visible from the previous one; HUD counter confirms",
  "photo cutouts are oversized boards in front of fences",
  "nothing structurally hidden: challenge is time"
 ],
 "designLogic": [
  "a bought level without a tape whose hardest content is timed lines on moving rides",
  "rides replace architecture as vert and rail pieces",
  "the letter tour is short (~36 s) and teaches the vertical stack",
  "tight clocks make failure cheap but frequent",
  "moving surfaces carry you to height (ferris wheel lip), echoing Shipyard's crane, Zoo's elephant, Chicago's bridge",
  "cutouts turn fences into collectibles",
  "the castle window is the one 'through' moment inside a combo",
  "arena dressing (banners) doubles as targets",
  "late-career score thresholds (750k / 1.5M) assume a finished main career",
  "easy line first (36 s S-K-A-T-E from spawn), hard line later on the same ground (0:30 ticket run)",
  "the theme supplies the collectibles: bell, photo cutouts, ride tickets read in-world"
 ],
 "remakeChanges": [
  "absent from THPS 3+4 (2025); only the 2002 PS2 design exists; no PS1 edition map"
 ],
 "transfer": [
  "Ferris-wheel crystal: lip-stall on a rotating wheel carriage (moving platform) from the bottom; crystal above the top carriage",
  "Coaster travelling rail with a moving car hazard following the hero; crystal at the bottom of the big hill",
  "Ticket line: 25-30 s line of shards ending in the crystal across a bowl",
  "Rocket-ride vert: swinging vert car with the crystal above the rim at the swing peak",
  "Castle window: wallride onto a castle wall whose grind passes through a window into an inner yard with the crystal"
 ],
